# These are byte-exact fixtures. Their sha256 is recorded in
# benchmark-manifest.json and in fusion-project.json's mesh_sources, and the
# test suite re-hashes every one of them on every run, so git must not touch a
# single byte on the way in or out. The repository normalises line endings by
# default (`* text=auto eol=lf` at the root); the vendor STEP files are CRLF
# exactly as their exporter wrote them and the ASCII STL is LF, and normalising
# either would change the digest the whole benchmark is bound to.
parts/*  -text
dumps/*  -text
